source: crates/harnx-script/src/description/tests.rs
expression: description
---
Chain this agent's tool commands and process their results in one script/round trip. This is an in-process shell, not host Bash. Only tool commands can reach host services, through their normal permissions and hooks.

Dialect: Bash-compatible BashKit. Fresh VFS per run, cwd /tmp; /attachments is read-only at /attachments/<full media CID> (keep existing CID encoding). No direct host filesystem, network or subprocess access. Pipes, redirects, variables, loops and background jobs (& / wait) work. set -e is on by default, with POSIX-style exceptions for conditions, ! and non-final &&/|| commands. Pipelines use the last command's status unless you enable set -o pipefail. Use set +e to handle ordinary failures; fatal errors still stop the script.

Available builtins (tool commands below override same-named builtins):
., :, [, alias, arch, assert, awk, b2sum, base32, base64, basename, basenc, bash, bc, bg, bind, break, builtin, bunzip2, busybox, bzcat, bzip2, caller, cat, cd, chgrp, chmod, chown, cksum, clear, cmp, column, comm, command, compgen, complete, compopt, continue, cp, csv, cut, date, dd, declare, df, diff, dirname, dirs, disown, dotenv, du, echo, egrep, enable, env, envsubst, eval, exec, exit, expand, export, expr, factor, false, fc, fg, fgrep, file, find, flock, fmt, fold, free, gawk, getconf, getopts, glob, grep, groups, gunzip, gzip, hash, head, help, hexdump, history, hostid, hostname, http, iconv, id, install, jobs, join, jq, json, kill, less, let, link, ln, local, locale, log, logname, ls, make, man, mapfile, mawk, md5sum, mkdir, mkfifo, mktemp, mv, nawk, nice, nl, nohup, nproc, numfmt, od, openssl, parallel, paste, patch, pgrep, pkill, popd, pr, printenv, printf, ps, pushd, pwd, python, python3, read, readarray, readlink, readonly, realpath, retry, return, rev, rg, rm, rmdir, sed, semver, seq, set, sh, sha1sum, sha224sum, sha256sum, sha384sum, sha512sum, shasum, shift, shopt, shuf, sleep, sort, source, split, stat, strings, sudo, sum, sync, tac, tail, tar, tee, template, test, timeout, times, tomlq, touch, tr, trap, tree, true, truncate, tsort, tty, type, typeset, ulimit, umask, unalias, uname, unexpand, uniq, unlink, unset, unzip, uptime, users, uuidgen, verify, wait, watch, wc, which, who, whoami, xargs, xxd, yes, yq, zip

Python: python and python3 are the same embedded Monty subset, not CPython. Use -c, a VFS script file or stdin/heredoc. open()/pathlib use the VFS. Simple classes work; inheritance, metaclasses, re and third-party imports don't. Python cannot call tools or start subprocesses/network requests; call tools in Bash and pass results via /tmp. A shared work budget caps scripts at ~95 Python calls; batch loops into one invocation.

Tool commands:
- files_fs_read --path <string> [--head-lines <integer>] [--json <object>]  # Read source files.
- media_attachment_create --content <string> --mime-type <string> [--encoding <string>] [--json <object>]  # Create an attachment.
- search --query <string> [--filter <json>] [--include-archived|--no-include-archived] [--tags <string>]... [--json <object>]  # Search indexed records.

Tool arguments/discovery:
- Property names become --kebab-case flags; strings/numbers take values, booleans use --flag / --no-flag, scalar arrays repeat flags, objects/complex values take quoted JSON. No positional arguments.
- --json '<object>' supplies original property keys; --json - reads stdin. Flags override base keys regardless of order. Stdin is otherwise ignored by tool commands.
- Output defaults to structuredContent JSON when present, otherwise text. -o json|text overrides rendering (not sent to the tool).
- tools [quoted-glob] lists synopses; help <tool> [tool ...] or <tool> --help shows full schema-derived help without dispatch.
- Tool exits: 0 success, 1 tool error, 2 usage, 3 needs approval (call directly instead), 4 blocked, 5 rejected, 127 unknown command. Run timeout: 124; cancellation: 130.

Quoting idioms:
- Literal multiline argument, with expansion inside the heredoc disabled:
```bash
text="$(cat <<'EOF'
literal $variables and "quotes"
EOF
)"
```
- Read text with "$(< /tmp/result.txt)" (command substitution strips trailing newlines).
- Batch arguments with xargs -n1; print shell-escaped values with printf '%q\n' "$text".
- Pass binary as base64 text: "$(base64 -w0 /tmp/x.png)".
- Create a PNG attachment from VFS bytes: `media_attachment_create --mime-type image/png --encoding base64 --content "$(base64 -w0 /tmp/x.png)"`.

Worked pipeline: Use a path this tool can read; filter matching lines and keep three:
```bash
files_fs_read --path src/lib.rs -o text | rg -n 'TODO' | head -3
```

Defaults/limits: timeout 86400s (timeout_secs: 0 disables it in practice); 10000 shell commands; stdout 1 MiB and stderr 1 MiB captured, with truncation flags/limit_hit. head_lines, tail_lines and max_output_bytes only shape the returned report. VFS: 10 MB per file, 100 MB total. Attachment mount: 10 MB per file, 100 MB cached per run; listings are empty, so use known full CIDs. Inner tools: 8 concurrent, 1000 admitted calls per script. Python: 64 MiB heap and print-buffer ceilings per invocation, bounded by remaining run time; MemoryError is stderr/exit 1, not a typed limit_hit. VM limits aren't process/RSS isolation.
